## Third-party references

This project was built by studying three open-source projects. Their
architectures and mathematics informed the design; no code was copied from any
of them. See `docs/ANALYSIS.md` for what was taken from each and
`docs/MIGRATION.md` §7 for the licence boundary.

| Project | Licence | What it contributed |
|---|---|---|
| `Trentct/m5stack-stopwatch-avatar` (KK) | AGPL-3.0 | Easing vocabulary, crossfade transitions, dirty-rectangle discipline for a small MCU. **Ideas only — no code copied.** |
| `ngocdevv/grok-bot-emoji` | MIT | The *principle* of a continuously morphing expression surface. No paths, colours or proportions used. |
| `MarcoFre/AURA---ESP32-S3-...` | MIT | State priority ladder, blink cadence, idle gesture table, audio envelope maths. |

The SphereWarp and DelayedFollow Rive effects by AB at Novra were supplied as a
reference by the project author, who states they are free to use. The sphere
projection in `src/avatar/core/sphere.ts` and the delayed-follow head spring in
`src/avatar/behaviors/body.ts` are ports of that maths.

### Note on AGPL

KK is AGPL-3.0. No KK source code appears in this repository, and the concepts
taken from it (easing functions, crossfade design, amplitude/period tuning) are
not copyrightable expression in any jurisdiction this project is distributed
into. If KK source is ever copied into the future StopWatch firmware, that
firmware becomes an AGPL-3.0 derivative and must be published under those terms.

All artwork in this repository — the grey sphere, the capsule eyes, the palette,
the gesture designs — is original to this project.
